{
  "id": "cross-modal-perception",
  "term": "cross-modal perception",
  "definition": "Cross-modal perception is perception that arises from combining information from different senses, especially hearing and vision, into one experience. In the context of visual music, the emotional impression can depend on how the auditory and visual signals fit together, and conflicting signals may make one sense dominate aspects of the perceived emotion.",
